      "writtenOn": "2026-11-18T02:22:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e excluding USB as MCTPUSBTarget covers this\n\nMy view is that using platform schema to describe USB MCTP endpoints is the wrong direction. This proposal is an alternative that allows USB devices to be described in a normal board configuration as the USB topology emerges from the connection of components.\n\n\u003e Can you explain how the following scenario be mapped.\n\nI haven\u0027t added examples specific to your circumstances, but I\u0027ve described the algorithm that I propose EM should use to resolve FRU EEPROM endpoints, which also applies to any other I2C device (e.g. MCTP devices). The algorithm handles any in-scope arrangement of muxes and ports. Please review that when I push it, and let me know if you need further clarification.",
      "parentUuid": "5a174322_4c8397de",
      "revId": "50cdd89482d6c93d7e4d8f3800883efa3aaa7b7a",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
