        "id": 1000009
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-18T02:22:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When mctpd discovers the presence of a non-local endpoint, which it may do by regularly polling EIDs handed out in pools it has allocated to bridges. In the case of a local endpoint it can publish the information directly as by definition there are no intervening bridges.\n\nHowever, under the proposal, we may also learn of MCTP devices that are bridged by EM announcing the existence of such a device. There may be ways we can use that information to be more intelligent about when polling occurs.",
      "parentUuid": "fde3e40d_56bf6d20",
      "revId": "50cdd89482d6c93d7e4d8f3800883efa3aaa7b7a",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
